---
import hero from '~/assets/images/logo-CPMM.png';

import claudio from '~/assets/images/claudio-parra.jpg';
import max from '~/assets/images/max-martinez.jpg';
---

<!-- ================= HERO ================= -->

<section
  id="home"
  class="relative h-[500px] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden"
>
  <img
    src={hero.src}
    alt="Principal Investigators"
    class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
  />

  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/50"></div>

  <div class="relative z-10 text-center px-6">
    <h1
      class="text-white font-extrabold leading-tight
             text-4xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
    >
      Principal Investigators
    </h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= CONTENT ================= -->

<section class="bg-white py-16">

  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-10 lg:px-20 space-y-36">

    <!-- ===================================================== -->
    <!-- CLAUDIO -->
    <!-- ===================================================== -->

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-16 items-start">

      <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->

      <div class="lg:col-span-4">

        <img
          src={claudio.src}
          alt="Dr. Claudio Parra"
          class="w-full rounded-md shadow-md"
        />

        <div class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-700">

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800">
            Dr. Claudio Parra
          </h2>

          <p>Assistant Professor</p>

          <p>Department of Organic Chemistry</p>

          <p>Faculty of Chemical Sciences</p>

          <p>University of Concepción</p>

          <div class="mt-1">

            <p>
              <strong>ORCID ID:</strong>
              <a
                href="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7356-2782"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-sky-700 hover:underline"
              >
                0000-0001-7356-2782
              </a>
            </p>

                        <p class="mt-1">
              <strong>Email:</strong>
              <a
                href="mailto:cparra@udec.cl"
                class="text-sky-700 hover:underline"
              >
                cparra@udec.cl
              </a>
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->

      <div class="lg:col-span-8">

        <p class="text-xl leading-10 text-gray-700 text-justify">

          Claudio Parra was born in Arica, Chile. He received his B.Sc. in Chemistry from the University of Tarapacá and subsequently earned an M.Sc. in Experimental and Industrial Organic Chemistry from the University of Barcelona (Spain). He then joined the research group of Prof. Josep Bonjoch at the University of Barcelona, where he completed his Ph.D. in Organic Chemistry. His doctoral research focused on the development of general asymmetric methods for the synthesis of key building blocks present in structurally complex polycyclic natural products. Following his doctoral studies, he carried out postdoctoral research with Dr. Ben Bradshaw at the University of Barcelona, where he expanded his expertise in synthetic methodology and complex molecule synthesis. He later founded and directed the Medicinal Chemistry and Natural Products Laboratory at the University of Tarapacá. He currently leads the Synthetic Methodology research line at CLab, University of Concepción.

        </p>

              </div>
              

    </div>
    
    <!-- ===================================================== -->
    <!-- MAX -->
    <!-- ===================================================== -->

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-16 items-start">

      <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->

      <div class="lg:col-span-4">

        <img
          src={max.src}
          alt="Dr. Max Martínez"
          class="w-full rounded-md shadow-md"
        />

        <div class="mt-8 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-700">

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-800">
            Dr. Max Martínez
          </h2>

          <p>Associate Professor</p>

          <p>Department of Organic Chemistry</p>

          <p>Faculty of Chemical Sciences</p>

          <p>University of Concepción</p>

          <div class="mt-1">

            <p>
              <strong>ORCID ID:</strong>
              0000-0000-0000-0000
            </p>

                        <p class="mt-1">
              <strong>Email:</strong>
              <a
                href="mailto:maxmartinez@udec.cl"
                class="text-sky-700 hover:underline"
              >
                maxmartinez@udec.cl
              </a>
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->

      <div class="lg:col-span-8">

        <p class="text-xl leading-10 text-gray-700 text-justify">

          Max Martínez was born in Santiago, Chile. He received his B.Sc. in Chemistry from the University of Chile. He then joined the research group of Prof. Ramiro Araya at the University of Chile, where he completed his Ph.D. in Organic Chemistry. His doctoral research focused on the synthesis of quinone and hydroquinone derivatives with antitumor activity. Following his doctoral studies, he carried out postdoctoral research with Dr. Leonardo Santos at the University of Talca, where he investigated curcumin derivatives with anticancer activity. He later joined the Metropolitan Technological University (UTEM) as a researcher, followed by appointments at Bernardo O'Higgins University and the University of Concepción. He currently serves as Associate Professor in the Department of Organic Chemistry, Faculty of Chemical Sciences, University of Concepción, where he leads the Computational Chemistry research line at CLab, University of Concepción.

        </p>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>